      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi+{sin}^{3}\u2061\\phi}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right)=8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi\\cdot ({cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right)\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi\\cdot ({cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi)}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right) & =8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi\\cdot 1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right) \\\\  & =8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\phi\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi+{sin}^{3}\u2061\\phi}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right)=8\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\phi.\n$$"
