      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi$ from the first two terms:\n\n$$\n8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\phi+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi+1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right)=8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi({sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi+{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi)+1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right)\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi({sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi+{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi)+1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right) & =8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi+1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right) \\\\  & =8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right) \\\\  & =8\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\phi+\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\phi\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n8\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{3}\u2061\\phi+\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\phi{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi+1}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi}\\right)=8\\cdot\\left(\\operatorname{tan}\u2061\\phi+\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\phi\\right)\n$$"
