      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{4}\u2061\\phi +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi {cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right)=2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi ({sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi )+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right)\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi ({sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi )+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right) & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\cdot 1+{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2\\cdot {sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }}{\\cancel{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\phi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot\\left(\\frac{{sin}^{4}\u2061\\phi +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi {cos}^{2}\u2061\\phi +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi }{{sin}^{2}\u2061\\phi \\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\phi }\\right)=4\\operatorname{sec}\u2061\\phi.\n$$"
